= Approach

Our five-member undergraduate project team combined interannual increments, EOF analysis, predictor selection, BiLSTM, and CSSPv2 to study precipitation and runoff prediction in the Yiluo River Basin. I contributed to the proposal and literature review, participated in predictor screening and prediction experiments, and learned to compile and run CSSPv2 and Fortran programs under guidance from Yumiao Wang.

= Team Results

The project materials report that three EOF components explained more than 90% of the precipitation-increment variance. Relative to statistical downscaling, the LSTM model improved temporal correlation by 16% and reduced RMSE by 20%; monthly runoff prediction achieved an NSE of 0.65. These are team results. The project completed its undergraduate innovation-program assessment and produced proposal, review, experiment, and presentation materials; no paper was published.
